caption: Quick Start — Overview
technology-rule: overview

Build any cybernetic in six decisions: concept, class, traits, support, access, and cost.

Use these six decisions before selecting individual implants. They keep the concept, traits, support, access, and limitations connected.

| Step | Question | What to Record |
| --- | --- | --- |
| 1. Concept | What should the cybernetic let the character do? | Restore, equip, enhance, or transform. |
| 2. Class | Can it pass casual inspection? Does it preserve the species body plan? | Class I covert, Class II anatomical, or Class III transformative. |
| 3. Traits | Which GURPS advantages and disadvantages create the effect? | List exact traits, levels, enhancements, and limitations. |
| 4. Support | What structure, power, cooling, neural control, and maintenance does it need? | Support level and required systems. |
| 5. Access | What TL, facility grade, legal class, license, and social reaction apply? | Minimum/mature TL, facility, LC, access tag. |
| 6. Cost | What is paid in points, money, time, debt, favors, or obligations? | Point cost, money band, surgery, recovery, maintenance. |

CORE RULE

Cybernetics are character traits with technological logistics. Money buys access; points buy reliable personal capability.
